Using LLM APIs with Smart Prompting — Step by Step

🧠 First, Understand the Core Idea
You don't need to train an AI. You need to instruct an existing AI (like Claude or GPT) very precisely so it behaves like your career counselor.
Think of it like hiring a brilliant expert — you just need to give them the right brief.

STEP 1 — Choose Your LLM API
APIBest ForCostClaude API (Anthropic)Long reasoning, nuanced adviceModerateGPT-4o (OpenAI)Most popular, good all-rounderModerateGemini API (Google)Free tier, good for India marketLow/Free

Recommendation: Start with Gemini API (generous free tier) for MVP. Switch or combine later.


STEP 2 — Understand "System Prompt" (Your Secret Weapon)
A system prompt is instructions you give the AI before the user talks to it. This is where you define its persona, rules, and knowledge.
You are CareerSaathi, a friendly AI career mentor for Indian 
10th and 12th standard students. 

You ONLY talk about:
- Career guidance
- Stream selection
- College options in India
- Entrance exams
- Scholarships

You speak in simple English. You are encouraging, never negative.
If a student scores low marks, you still show them positive paths.
You always give answers relevant to Indian education system.
This single prompt transforms a general AI into YOUR specialized career counselor.

STEP 3 — Design Smart Prompt Templates
For each feature, you pre-write a prompt template and fill in student data dynamically.
Example — Career Recommendation:
javascriptconst prompt = `
  Student Profile:
  - Class: ${student.class}          // "12th"
  - Stream: ${student.stream}        // "Science"
  - Marks: ${student.marks}          // "65%"
  - Interests: ${student.interests}  // "Drawing, Gaming"
  - Location: ${student.city}        // "Pune"
  - Budget: ${student.budget}        // "Under 5 LPA fees"

  Task: Suggest top 5 career options for this student.
  
  For each career, provide:
  1. Career name
  2. Why it suits this student (2 lines)
  3. Required entrance exam
  4. Top 3 affordable colleges near ${student.city}
  5. Expected starting salary
  6. Future demand (High/Medium/Low)
  
  Respond in JSON format.
`;
You just fill the variables — AI does the heavy thinking.

STEP 4 — Ask AI to Respond in JSON
This is critical. Always ask for structured output so your frontend can render it properly.
javascriptconst systemPrompt = `
  Always respond in valid JSON only. 
  No extra explanation outside JSON.
`;

// API Call Example (using Gemini or OpenAI)
const response = await fetch("https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages", {
  method: "POST",
  headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
  body: JSON.stringify({
    model: "claude-sonnet-4-20250514",
    system: systemPrompt,
    messages: [{ role: "user", content: prompt }],
    max_tokens: 1000
  })
});

const result = await response.json();
const careerData = JSON.parse(result.content[0].text);
// Now render careerData on your UI cards

